ty_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":31,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Summary**\n\n**What I changed and why.** The delivered network differs from the original in only the output biases of the two NS phases, each raised by 0.5. The training demand carried a random directional bias whose average favoured EW over NS by about 10%, while the test demand is unbiased. On the recorded states, a 10% shift in the NS/EW input ratio moves the net's own NS-versus-EW logit preference by 0.53, so +0.5 is the net's own scale for that correction. It flips about 2% of honoured decisions.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 2 of 7428.\n\n**Simulator calls:** 7 of 10. A constructed \"stay bonus\" (a phase-level unit plus three threshold decoders, 317 params) caused lock-in at high demand (143 and 1107 veh-h). A time-gated version was safe but neutral (44.55, 44.64). The baseline scored 44.51. The NS bias gave 44.48 at +0.5 and 44.61 at +1.0. All differences other than the lock-ins are within the dev noise of about ±0.3 veh-h.\n\n**Dev TTS of final weights:** 44.48 veh-h (low 34.5, nominal 44.9, high 54.0), no vehicles left.\n\n**Test predictions:** low 34.5, nominal 44.8, high 54.2 veh-h. Honest expectation: roughly equal to the original, with the edit justified by the demand-bias argument rather than a measured gain.","ttft_ms":2758,"type":"result","duration_ms":998633,"uuid":"2c4f8a83-43b7-4f76-8356-06114f6c58b0","ttft_stream_ms":2185,"time_to_request_ms":64,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":10,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":5,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":3,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":4,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":5,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":4,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","proces